{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Blessed.</b> It returns to explain that the prayer he prayed to bless them will be fulfilled." "<b>And the sense of \"maker of heaven and earth\"</b> — that He established the dry land and the firmament, as in: \"on the day that YHWH Elohim made earth and heaven\" (Genesis 2:4). And behold, the sense is that He rules over the high and the low, and He will bless you."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 115, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:39:44.409520737Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}